<title>JAPAN: Most appropriate level 120 yen to dlr - LDP official.</title>
<headline>Most appropriate level 120 yen to dlr - LDP official.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>An exchange rate of around 120 yen to the dollar is the most appropriate level, a senior official of Japan's ruling Liberal Democratic Party said on Monday.</p>
<p>Taku Yamasaki, chairman of the LDP's policy research council, also told reporters he does see the yen weakening for some time.  </p>
<p>&quot;I don't think there will be a weaker yen for some time. I think around 120 yen is the most appropriate,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
